# CYP2C19*2 Variant Information

## 1. Gene Overview

**Gene symbol:** CYP2C19  
**Full name:** Cytochrome P450 Family 2 Subfamily C Member 19  
**Chromosomal location:** Chromosome 10q23.33  
**Gene function:** Encodes a cytochrome P450 enzyme involved in the metabolism of several clinically important drugs.

CYP2C19 belongs to the cytochrome P450 superfamily of enzymes, which participate in the oxidative metabolism of endogenous compounds and xenobiotics, including therapeutic drugs.

One of its important pharmacological functions is contributing to the metabolic activation of clopidogrel, an antiplatelet prodrug.

